@page "/"

<PageTitle>CargoPulse · Foundation</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Production-oriented foundation</p>
    <h1>The control tower has a reliable place to stand.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
        The API, background worker and Blazor host share health checks, structured logs,
        trace propagation and service discovery. Shipment workflows are intentionally not
        simulated before their domain model exists.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="status-grid" aria-label="Foundation status">
    <article>
        <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h2>API host</h2>
        <p>Problem Details, OpenAPI, correlation IDs, rate limiting and readiness probes.</p>
        <code>/health · /ready</code>
    </article>
    <article>
        <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h2>Worker host</h2>
        <p>A separate restart-safe process boundary with a monitored heartbeat.</p>
        <code>worker_heartbeat_timestamp_seconds</code>
    </article>
    <article>
        <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h2>Local infrastructure</h2>
        <p>PostgreSQL and RabbitMQ are wired through Aspire or Docker Compose.</p>
        <code>at-least-once planned · not exactly-once</code>
    </article>
</section>

<section class="next-step">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Next milestone</p>
        <h2>Carriers and shipments</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
        Milestone 1 introduces the first domain aggregates, PostgreSQL migrations and the
        shipment state machine. Until then, this screen reports foundation scope honestly.
    </p>
</section>
